{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904182-spirit-rituals-for-vampires","id":904182,"title":"Spirit rituals for vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-31T08:36:10-07:00","id":904182,"title":"Spirit rituals for vampires","content":"So, my setting has a bloodline of vampires, the Hetkepu, that deal with spirits using the Blood Tenebrous Discipline. After dealing with temporal concerns for several years, my Hetkepu player has recently started spreading her wings in the family business. Now some of the bits of lore and rituals I put together and set aside are relevant again. If I may, I will post some of the ideas and see what options there are for tweaking them.<br /> <br /> First, here is a spirit receptacle that is more condo than fetish. Please note that the terminology hasn\u2019t been updated to 2<sup>nd</sup> Ed. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ushabti (</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Ritual)</b><br /> <br /> An Ushabti is a statuette made to resemble an animal or human. Ancient Egyptians used these to represent the spirits who would serve them in the afterlife. Egyptian vampires use them as homes for the spirits that serve them in this world. <br /> <br /> The ritualist (usually one who also knows Blood Tenebrous) creates a figure from wood, clay, stone, or metal (only a few would use plastic in modern times) representing a particular spirit he wishes to bind to his service, while chanting or singing the proper formulae. The figure should either resemble the spirit\u2019s normal form or be representative of the spirit\u2019s purpose (so that an owl spirit\u2019s ushabti should look like an owl, while that of a spirit of battle might look like a human warrior). On the bottom is written the name the spirit goes by. Once the ushabti-creation ritual is completed, the ritualist may then summon the appropriate spirit, make suitable offerings, and explain what he wishes. Negotiations ensue. If the spirit agrees, it enters the ushabti and claims it.<br /> <br /> There are several significant advantages to the ushabti. First, it gives the particular spirit access through the gauntlet without using its own energy. Secondly, it acts as a fetter to allow it to stay safely in the material world. Third, the effigy produces a point of Essence each day, provided the spirit resides in the object for an hour or so. No other spirit can use these advantages, meaning the spirit has a hiding place and sustenance. In return, of course, it must serve the ritualist. Usually this is as a spy, or a guardian during daysleep or torpor. Other services are possible, of course, limited only to the willingness of available spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Roll: </b>Craft + Occult + Hekau<br /> <b>Modifiers:</b> Hastily made item (-2), Particularly appropriate material (+1), Extra care in making the item (double the crafting time) (+1)<br /> <b>Actions:</b> Extended. 3 Successes per Rank of the desired spirit. Time increment depends on the material used (carving and then painting marble will take longer than carving soft wood). <br /> <b> Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Whether its name was misspelled or the likeness is unflattering, the spirit is offended by the offering, and will harass the ritualist.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The item is worthless to the spirit.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The ushabti is acceptable to the spirit, giving a +1 to ritualist for purposes of negotiations. The spirit can thereafter enter the ushabti and receive the benefits outlined above. <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: As above, but also gives 2 Essence per day. The ritualist derives +2 bonus dice to negotiate with the spirit.<br /> <br /> <i>Example: Amunhotep the Hetkepu wishes Hood of Death, a greater gaffling, to guard his tomb while he sleeps during the day. Out of 2-foot length of ebony he carves the figure of a cobra poised to strike, taking extra care to get the details right (The ST determines the action interval for the hard wood is 1 night, so extra care will increase that to 2 nights). A greater gaffling is a Rank Two spirit, requiring 2x3 successes. The player rolls Craft+Occult+Hekau (2+2+4)+2 for extra time, netting 4 successes for two nights work. In two more nights of work, he gains an additional 5 successes, for a total of 9. That is a net of 3 successes. Amunhotep finishes with the spirit\u2019s name on the underside of the figurine, and the player marks off a Willpower point. Presenting the ushabti during his meeting with Hood of Death will sweeten the deal, giving the vampire a bonus die.</i><br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:40:51-07:00","id":905476,"title":"","content":"Though it deals with spirits this may belong more on the vampire section.<br /> <br /> My main feedback that I can give is I think that a point of willpower is far too little a price for what you are presenting. I'd suggest requiring a vitae that came from feeding on a spirit with a bonus for if the spirit resonates with the initial essance and a penalty if it is a polar opposite. There is a merit to allow a vampire to feed on spirits. If they are dealing with spirits in such a way as this they should have a way to acess spirits in a temporary way to gain this vitae to fuel a longer stay.<br /> <br /> Being able to negate the difficulty of crossing the gauntlet and effectively giving the spirit an anchor also seems to be too much. I like the idea of the spiritual anchor and how one would barter for service in exchange but to have this on top of pulling it effortlessly across the gauntlet is too much. My suggestion here would be to penalize based on the gauntlet strength as a spirit would be to cross over themself where you are. So doing so at a locus would impose no penalty while in the middle of a city would impose quite a penalty. <br /> <br /> So, a vampire should not be better than a werewolf with calling spirits and so should have to jump through more hoops.<br /> <br /> Edit: also how long does this totem retain its potency? It seems to be permanent, it shouldn't be permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T05:47:34-07:00","id":905561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904182-spirit-rituals-for-vampires?p=905476#post905476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though it deals with spirits this may belong more on the vampire section.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a toss-up. I decided that since the ritual could just as easily be used by a mortal sorcerer, it would be best to post where people are most familiar with the spirit mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My main feedback that I can give is I think that a point of willpower is far too little a price for what you are presenting. I'd suggest requiring a vitae that came from feeding on a spirit with a bonus for if the spirit resonates with the initial essance and a penalty if it is a polar opposite. There is a merit to allow a vampire to feed on spirits. If they are dealing with spirits in such a way as this they should have a way to acess spirits in a temporary way to gain this vitae to fuel a longer stay. </div> </div> </div>Fair point on the willpower. I might even go with a Will dot. As to the vitae, Blood Tenebrous allows you to convert Vitae to Essence, so I figured that would be in play for this particular use of the ritual.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being able to negate the difficulty of crossing the gauntlet and effectively giving the spirit an anchor also seems to be too much. I like the idea of the spiritual anchor and how one would barter for service in exchange but to have this on top of pulling it effortlessly across the gauntlet is too much. My suggestion here would be to penalize based on the gauntlet strength as a spirit would be to cross over themself where you are. So doing so at a locus would impose no penalty while in the middle of a city would impose quite a penalty. </div> </div> </div>That would work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, a vampire should not be better than a werewolf with calling spirits and so should have to jump through more hoops. </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Although this particular bloodline of vampires is unique in its ability to deal with spirits \u2013 which is causing confusion and a bit of animosity with the local werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: also how long does this totem retain its potency? It seems to be permanent, it shouldn't be permanent. </div> </div> </div>Why not? If a given spirit has a nest/anchor that it uses habitually, the item should become more comfortable and form-fitting as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:12:01-07:00","id":905739,"title":"","content":"If you want to keep it as I permanent the I'd suggest it to cost a willpower dot. Since it only costs 1xp compared to 1e it isn't too steep of a cost. Otherwise I'd suggest needing to reinforce the ritual maybe month. Reinforcing it would of course be easier than the initial ritual and probably either only take one roll or one night.<br /> <br /> If the bloodline can convert vitae to essance then an essance cost would be easy to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}